      "source": [
        "### 7.4 Evaluación cuantitativa: KID\n",
        "El *Kernel Inception Distance* compara las características de InceptionV3 de imágenes reales y generadas (MMD² con kernel polinomial). Es la métrica que usa el ejemplo oficial de Keras de DDIM sobre este mismo dataset y, a diferencia del FID, es insesgada con pocas muestras. **Más bajo es mejor.** Como referencia calculamos también el KID entre dos grupos de imágenes reales (el “piso”) y entre ruido y reales (el “techo”)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "d8801805",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d8801805"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "N_KID = 500\n",
        "inception = keras.applications.InceptionV3(include_top=False, pooling=\"avg\",\n",
        "                                           weights=\"imagenet\", input_shape=(299, 299, 3))\n",
        "\n",
        "def inception_features(images_0_255, bs=25):\n",
        "    feats = []\n",
        "    for i in range(0, len(images_0_255), bs):\n",
        "        x = ops.image.resize(ops.convert_to_tensor(images_0_255[i:i + bs], dtype=\"float32\"), (299, 299))\n",
        "        x = keras.applications.inception_v3.preprocess_input(x)\n",
        "        feats.append(ops.convert_to_numpy(inception(x, training=False)))\n",
        "    return np.concatenate(feats).astype(np.float64)\n",
        "\n",
        "def kid(f1, f2):\n",
        "    d, m = f1.shape[1], min(len(f1), len(f2))\n",
        "    f1, f2 = f1[:m], f2[:m]\n",
        "    kxx, kyy, kxy = (f1 @ f1.T / d + 1) ** 3, (f2 @ f2.T / d + 1) ** 3, (f1 @ f2.T / d + 1) ** 3\n",
        "    return float((kxx.sum() - np.trace(kxx)) / (m * (m - 1))\n",
        "                 + (kyy.sum() - np.trace(kyy)) / (m * (m - 1)) - 2 * kxy.mean())\n",
        "\n",
        "real = np.concatenate([b.numpy() for b in dataset.take(2 * N_KID // batch_size + 1)])[: 2 * N_KID]\n",
        "chunks = [100] * (N_KID // 100) + ([N_KID % 100] if N_KID % 100 else [])\n",
        "gen = np.concatenate([ops.convert_to_numpy(model.generate(c, 20)) for c in chunks])\n",
        "noise_imgs = np.random.uniform(0, 255, gen.shape).astype(\"float32\")\n",
        "\n",
        "f_real_a, f_real_b = inception_features(real[:N_KID]), inception_features(real[N_KID:])\n",
        "f_gen, f_noise = inception_features(gen), inception_features(noise_imgs)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"KID real vs real (piso) : {kid(f_real_a, f_real_b):.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"KID generadas vs reales : {kid(f_gen, f_real_a):.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"KID ruido vs reales     : {kid(f_noise, f_real_a):.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
